| `scripts/corpus_level.py` | The one reader of the level a file states on disk: the corpus build's frontmatter and module-docstring grammars, the one read of a README.md's level, which `scripts/check_structure.py` re-exports for check_A, the README.md chain a file takes its level from, and `stated_now`, which reads a file again so `scripts/query_corpus.py`, the agents and the showcase's node detail decide on the level the file states now as well as the corpus's (`config_loader.is_served_now`). | imported; `scripts/jobs/build_corpus.py` reads each node's README.md levels through it | [`corpus.served_visibilities`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Ranks nothing: the vocabulary and the strictest-wins rule are `scripts/config_loader.py`'s. A file it cannot read, a Markdown file with no frontmatter, a module with no docstring and any other kind of file have no level, which a reader serves as nothing. Stays stdlib-only and 3.6-safe, because it sits in the bottom import layer. | [CONVENTIONS.md](../../CONVENTIONS.md) | always |
